    "revision": 1,
    "title": "Write a practical message",
    "subtitle": "The intention was different · 1 · preparation 1",
    "context": "Use this subset of the feelings vocabulary and constructions in a short self-contained situation, preparing for U4-23. Use the selected vocabulary and constructions to distinguish an expressed attitude from an assumption and repair a misunderstanding.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-CORE-U4-23-P01-compose-produce",
        "kind": "check",
        "title": "Compose a purposeful message",
        "questions": [
          {
            "id": "EX-CORE-U4-23-P01-compose-draft",
            "kind": "production",
            "response": "written",
            "prompt": "The intention was different · 1 · preparation 1: Write a short handover for an absent participant. Explain the request or problem, the response, and what has changed or remains unresolved.",
            "promptLanguage": "en",
            "context": "周末有比赛，朋友问我要不要一起参加，我却在手机上回他：我才不去呢。他很快说知道了，以后不再问。我有点儿奇怪，因为我只是开玩笑，本来准备说当然要去。\n\n见面以后，他说那些字看着很不高兴，像是不想他再问我要不要去。我这才发现，自己说时脸上有笑，他看见的却只是字，没有听见我开玩笑的声音。\n\n我告诉他，我并不是不想去，还拿出比赛需要的东西给他看。他说早一点儿这样说就清楚了。我没有让他必须知道我在开玩笑，而是先把要不要去说清楚。\n\n我问以后是不是都不能开玩笑，他说不是，这次只是要决定我们是不是一起去。先给一个能帮助安排的回答，再开玩笑，就不会让他不知道该等还是自己走。\n\n比赛那天，我按时到了。朋友笑着说，以为我会再来一句不去。我也笑了，但是这次先告诉他，已经准备好了，现在就可以出发。\n\n后来，用手机开玩笑以前，我会先想一下，对方看到这些字会怎么想。我觉得好笑，对方却不一定觉得好笑。对方说不定会以为我不想去，所以重要的事要先说清楚。",
            "contextLanguage": "zh",
            "label": "Write your own message",
            "resultDomain": "Self-reviewed writing practice",
            "rubric": [
              {
                "id": "r1",
                "text": "The reader can distinguish the request, response and current situation."
              },
              {
                "id": "r2",
                "text": "My account attributes the relevant statements to the correct people."
              }
            ],
            "minLength": 1
          }
        ],
        "sequential": true
      }
